  "limits": [
    "The native capture calls public SDK closest-point queries only. It does not execute PointDeviation or capture the native panel, analysis mesh sampling, defaults, color/proximity policies, population-vs-sample statistics policy or permanent-layer behavior. The captured statistics are independently derived from SDK distances. Local behavior is documented explicitly; full native command/panel parity is unqualified.",
    "All 65 recorded paired closest locations pass exact squared-distance admission at 1e-6. Distances, target indices and five derived scalar statistics agree. This finite corpus does not establish a continuous nearest-point or ambiguous/tied-location equivalence proof for arbitrary geometry. Underlying query failures reject the analysis rather than substituting a mesh approximation for a target surface.",
    "Source curves use equal arc-length divisions, adding missing polyline vertices; surface/B-rep sources use the existing display tessellator. Every stored mesh/cloud vertex contributes, including orphan vertices and duplicates. Source sampling can differ from Rhino. Block/SubD/instance expansion is not implemented by this command.",
    "The statistics population excludes distances greater than Ignore. IgnoreBad and proximity filter only display hairs. Proximity uses the curve normal plane or either surface/mesh normal; an undefined normal hides a nonzero hair below 180 degrees. Singular-normal and native boundary-color policies remain unqualified.",
    "MakePermanent uses displayed exaggerated nonzero segments and Point Test RGB layers. Existing line construction can reject short segments, and nonrepresentable exaggeration rejects atomically. Read-only reports preserve model history and Redo. Closing the panel hides it while retaining the analysis; End releases the samples and caches.",
    "Runtime tests and the local export use default debug builds. Clippy checks every workspace target with native-smlib enabled. No native C++ was changed and no sanitizer or benchmark is claimed. Raw timing fields include different wrappers and are not a performance qualification.",
    "The first capture failed before SDK execution because a shared probe imported pathlib in Rhino IronPython. The helper now uses portable os/open, finite-value checks and string types. The second capture completed all 14 recipes and 65 closest queries. An intermediate test run hit a missing rustdoc artifact while Cargo jobs shared the target directory; the final sequential regression run completed successfully. No Wine, FEX or license configuration was changed."
  ],
